Power tree regulation testbench (generated per sweep point)
.include models.lib

* 12V input source (swept)
V1 VIN_12V GND DC {{vin}}

* U1: 12V -> 5V intermediate. Everything else hangs off this node, so its
* load is the sum of all downstream conversion, reflected through EFF.
X1 VIN_12V GND PLUS5V REG PARAMS: VSET=5.0 RS=0.005 LINEREG=0.005 EFF=0.90
* Camera module, switched pass-through of +5V (200mA budgeted)
Rload5 PLUS5V GND 25.0

* U2: 5V -> 3.3V always-on system rail (supervisor + housekeeping, 50mA)
X2 PLUS5V GND PLUS3V3S REG PARAMS: VSET=3.3 RS=0.02 EFF=0.88
Rload3s PLUS3V3S GND 66.0

* U3: 5V -> 3.3V gated FPGA VCCIO rail (50mA budgeted)
X3 PLUS5V GND PLUS3V3F REG PARAMS: VSET=3.3 RS=0.02 EFF=0.90
Rload3f PLUS3V3F GND 66.0

* U4: 5V -> 2.5V VCCAUX. LDO, so EFF is Vout/Vin (25mA budgeted).
X4 PLUS5V GND PLUS2V5 REG PARAMS: VSET=2.5 RS=0.05 EFF=0.50
Rload2v5 PLUS2V5 GND 100.0

* U5: 5V -> 1.1V VCC core, load swept from the 250mA budgeted worst case
* (4.4 ohm) out to the 77mA static-only floor (14.3 ohm).
X5 PLUS5V GND PLUS1V1 REG PARAMS: VSET=1.1 RS=0.02 EFF=0.85
Rloadcore PLUS1V1 GND {{rload_core}}

.control
op
print v(PLUS5V)
print v(PLUS3V3S)
print v(PLUS3V3F)
print v(PLUS2V5)
print v(PLUS1V1)
.endc
.end
